IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`
IMPORT `cbr-reg1`

-- TESTS OF REGULATION 1. Every expected value is written from the text (src:4, 9,
-- 13-15, 16) before the run, and is not copied from the encoding's own output.

§ `Tests of regulation 1`

§§ `The dates (src:4, src:9)`

-- "Made 29th March 2006"
#ASSERT `the date these Regulations were made` EQUALS Date 29 3 2006
-- "shall come into force on 10th April 2006"
#ASSERT `the date these Regulations come into force` EQUALS Date 10 4 2006

-- In force from 10 April 2006 on its first day: the boundary on both sides.
#ASSERT `these Regulations are in force in the week beginning` (Date 10 4 2006)
#ASSERT NOT (`these Regulations are in force in the week beginning` (Date 9 4 2006))
#ASSERT `these Regulations are in force in the week beginning` (Date 11 4 2006)
-- The day they were made is before they came into force.
#ASSERT NOT (`these Regulations are in force in the week beginning` (Date 29 3 2006))
-- Far after.
#ASSERT `these Regulations are in force in the week beginning` (Date 1 6 2026)

-- Not a provision of the text: the version date (../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2006-965.meta.json, "version: 2026-04-06").
#ASSERT `the date of the version of the text encoded` EQUALS Date 6 4 2026

§§ `"qualifying young person" (src:13-15): a person in Great Britain who is one under Part 9 of SSCBA, or in Northern Ireland under Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A`

-- Limb (a): in Great Britain, and such a person for the purposes of SSCBA.
#ASSERT `a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` `in Great Britain` TRUE FALSE
-- In Great Britain, but only the Northern Ireland test is met: limb (a) is not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` `in Great Britain` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` `in Great Britain` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` `in Great Britain` FALSE FALSE)
-- Limb (b): in Northern Ireland, and such a person for the purposes of SSCB(NI)A.
#ASSERT `a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` `in Northern Ireland` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` `in Northern Ireland` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` `in Northern Ireland` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` `in Northern Ireland` FALSE FALSE)
-- Elsewhere: neither limb reaches the person, whatever Part 9 says.
#ASSERT NOT (`a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` `in neither Great Britain nor Northern Ireland` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` `in neither Great Britain nor Northern Ireland` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Regulation 1(3) (src:16): facts are tested at the beginning of that week`

#ASSERT `the day on which conditions and facts are tested in the week beginning` (Date 6 4 2026) EQUALS Date 6 4 2026
#ASSERT `the day on which conditions and facts are tested in the week beginning` (Date 13 4 2026) EQUALS Date 13 4 2026
